    "assignees": [],
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "## Summary\n\n- Negotiate response coding from the request's `Accept-Encoding` instead of always claiming `br`.\n- JIT compression (`--compress`, including transpiled SCSS/TS output) now only applies brotli when the client accepts it; otherwise the response is sent uncompressed.\n- Pre-compressed sibling files are served only when their coding is accepted, preferring `.br` over `.gz` consistent with the header's quality values.\n- Compressed variants now send `Vary: Accept-Encoding` so shared caches keep separate entries.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `cargo test --workspace`\n- `cargo clippy --all-targets --workspace -- -D warnings`\n- `cargo xfmt --check`\n\nFixes #22\n",
